### **Root Cause**

The `Spacing` transform in MONAI uses interpolation to resample the image to the new pixel spacing. By default, the `align_corners` parameter is set to `False`, which means the corners of the input and output tensors are treated as referring to the corner points of the input’s corner pixels. This can lead to a mismatch in the physical extent when the resampling factors are not integers or when the spacing changes significantly.

